&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Retail Associate to join our London team. Our ideal candidate is warm and curious, with a natural instinct for service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work in an ambitious environment where we are reimagining what modern luxury can feel like, sharing your knowledge of our products with care and acting as a true ambassador for everything Tekla stands for.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The primary location for this position is Marylebone High Street, though occasional support at our Selfridges counter, a short walk from the store, may also be required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should enjoy taking on responsibility and feel a genuine interest in understanding what each customer needs. A real appreciation for our brand and for premium product, paired with an eagerness to learn and to share what you know, will be at the heart of your success here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time position, and because of the rhythm of the store, availability during evenings and weekends is essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every day in this role looks a little different, but you can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build genuine, lasting relationships with our customers through thoughtful clienteling, making each visit feel personal and unhurried.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Host our VIP clients in store and at private appointments, offering informed advice with care and discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the store&#39;s daily operations, including sales, visual merchandising, and replenishment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of our products and how to care for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share regular reporting and customer feedback with the store manager and senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work both independently and with the team to ensure the day runs smoothly and to meet our shared goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on other ad hoc duties as and when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We would love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a customer-facing role, ideally within premium or luxury retail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in clienteling, from personalised follow-ups to building a loyal client base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of premium product: what sets it apart, and how to speak about it with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience hosting VIP clients at a high level and reporting feedback to senior management would be advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, detail-oriented approach, with a genuine interest in helping others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Warmth, curiosity, and the ability to start conversations and build relationships with customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and the confidence to adapt to different customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability to work weekends and evenings when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine appreciation for our brand and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We review applications and hold interviews on an ongoing basis, with the aim of welcoming the successful candidate to the role as soon as possible.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;We’re on a mission to become the go-to destination for students across Europe to find a trusted home away from home. We make every step of the rental journey simple and seamless, so students can focus on what really matters: studying, exploring, and growing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With HousingAnywhere, Kamernet, and Studapart under our roof, we’re Europe’s largest student rental platform. You’ll find us in Rotterdam, Paris, and Cergy, always guided by our four core values: Ownership, We are enablers, We are changemakers, and We are connectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To support our continued growth, we are creating a new, strategic role at the heart of operational performance and customer experience. There is no Quality &amp;amp; Training activity in the Group today : you will build it from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Quality &amp;amp; Training Manager, you will create and lead the Quality &amp;amp; Training activity for the whole HousingAnywhere Group, covering the Operations teams in Cergy and Rotterdam. You define its scope, methods and tools, and you are responsible for service quality and operational practices across the Group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You work closely with the managers of the Customer Support and Booking Ops teams to structure training, onboarding, quality monitoring and performance tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is based in France, with frequent travel to our Rotterdam office. English is the main working language.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building the Quality &amp;amp; Training activity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the Quality &amp;amp; Training activity : scope, operating model, priorities and roadmap,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up the tools, rituals and governance needed to run the activity at Group level,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Harmonise quality and training practices between the Cergy and Rotterdam teams,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lay the foundations for the activity to grow as needs evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training &amp;amp; onboarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify the training needs of the Ops teams, and accompany the integration process while migrating to a single operating model in 2027,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop complete training programmes covering customer service posture, tools, and day-to-day processes and procedures,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain training materials (scripts, practical guides, process sheets, e-learning content), working with the other departments like Product for new features,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a structured onboarding and support new joiners in live situations after initial training, to bridge theory and practice,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry out an individual assessment at the end of onboarding (audits, call listening, double listening, tests) and provide personalised follow-up,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead group and one-to-one sessions, on-the-spot debriefs and targeted coaching on the fundamentals: call handling, request qualification, rephrasing, quality of written and spoken answers, and CRM data entry,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train teams on new procedures and tool changes as they are rolled out.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
